                    Sirach commends humility, docility, and work within one's capacity while warning against presumption and inquiry beyond what is entrusted. This is not a command against learning; it is a correction of pride that treats limits as insults. Proverbs praises the prudent person who sees danger and takes refuge. Seeking shelter is not cowardice when shelter preserves life and future responsibility. A person leaving an abusive setting, evacuating a disaster, using protective equipment, or withdrawing from an unwinnable argument may be choosing the difficult good rather than avoiding it.

